+/**
+ * Structured-data capability bundle (v2).
+ *
+ * Observed-run evidence drove this composition shape:
+ *
+ *  1. In the scored baseline runs the executor never called `data_read` or
+ *     `data_write`; it read inputs with `read`/`bash` and committed outputs with
+ *     the generic `write` tool. A capability the model does not select cannot
+ *     contribute, so v2 registers system-prompt guidance naming these tools at
+ *     the point where the generic file tools are documented.
+ *  2. A probe showed the generic `write` tool renders only "Created file" /
+ *     "Updated file": the committed value never reaches the caller. Two
+ *     consecutive baseline runs therefore could not observe the bytes they
+ *     believed they had written. v2 owns the whole commit path *inside one
+ *     handler*: `data_write` (whole value, with written-bytes receipt) and
+ *     `data_replace` (targeted, fs-observation-policy-respecting repair that
+ *     reports the resulting digest), plus a guidance section that routes
+ *     whole-value commits through `data_write`.
+ *  3. A guard that wrapped the tool runtime's scheduler was probed in the
+ *     native profile and had no effect: `TOOL_RUNTIME_SCHEDULER` is an own
+ *     instance field of the shipped ToolRuntime, so reassigning it cannot
+ *     intercept dispatch. v2 contains no such mechanism; only supported
+ *     extension points (tool registration, system-prompt sections) are used.
+ *
+ * Tools:
+ *  - `data_read`    verbatim UTF-8 read that cites exact bytes (size + SHA-256).
+ *  - `data_write`   commits caller-supplied JSON to an explicit /workspace file
+ *                   and reports bytes, digest and top-level keys written.
+ *  - `data_replace` exact literal replacement in an existing text file, with
+ *                   optional occurrence count and parsed-JSON validation.
+ *  - `data_verify`  checks one file against an explicit declared shape and
+ *                   returns computed facts; never edits or guesses intent.
+ *
+ * No task identifier, fixture value or expected answer is encoded here; every
+ * reported fact is computed from the bytes actually on disk.
+ */
+
